Can I ask you guys something?

284
00:15:12,377 --> 00:15:13,854
Well...

285
00:15:13,937 --> 00:15:16,017
What did you all think at first?

286
00:15:16,517 --> 00:15:17,917
About the two of us dating.

287
00:15:22,577 --> 00:15:27,257
Honestly, I was
definitely surprised at first.

288
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,294
But...

289
00:15:29,377 --> 00:15:31,537
guys are always super close anyway.

290
00:15:32,297 --> 00:15:36,385
Once I saw it as an extension
of that, it didn't really bother me.

291
00:15:37,317 --> 00:15:38,997
Or rather, it made sense to me.

292
00:15:40,137 --> 00:15:43,167
I don't really get the
romantic part of it yet,

293
00:15:43,997 --> 00:15:46,997
but I totally get feeling more
comfortable around guys.

294
00:15:51,977 --> 00:15:52,977
Oh.

295
00:15:53,777 --> 00:15:55,334
As for me, as long as it's not me,

296
00:15:55,417 --> 00:15:56,417
I couldn't care less.

297
00:15:56,837 --> 00:15:58,214
Trying to act cool?

298
00:15:58,297 --> 00:15:59,297
Huh?

299
00:15:59,377 --> 00:16:00,974
You say that,

300
00:16:01,057 --> 00:16:03,377
when you're clearly the one
who's most worried about them.

301
00:16:03,457 --> 00:16:04,654
As if! No way.

302
00:16:04,737 --> 00:16:05,794
You totally were.

303
00:16:05,877 --> 00:16:06,993
Even back at the training camp.

304
00:16:07,017 --> 00:16:07,734
Hey, wait.

305
00:16:07,817 --> 00:16:08,551
Stop talking!

306
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,273
- Sorry, my bad, I'm sorry!
- "What's going on with Watarai and Hioki?"

307
00:16:10,297 --> 00:16:11,638
Ow, I said I'm sorry...

308
00:16:11,721 --> 00:16:13,914
Oh, wait, wait...

309
00:16:13,997 --> 00:16:15,014
I'm heading out.

310
00:16:15,097 --> 00:16:17,177
- "Wait, Hioki and Watarai..."
- Where are you going?

311
00:16:20,797 --> 00:16:21,797
Um...

312
00:16:22,797 --> 00:16:25,037
There's something I want
to ask you too, Watarai.

313
00:16:26,379 --> 00:16:27,379
Yeah?

314
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:29,155
What is it?

315
00:16:31,737 --> 00:16:33,137
It's about Suzu-san.

316
00:16:34,877 --> 00:16:37,497
Like how things were when you were dating.

317
00:16:38,157 --> 00:16:39,697
Do you mind if I ask?

318
00:16:41,977 --> 00:16:43,277
Sure.

319
00:16:47,517 --> 00:16:48,817
We started dating

320
00:16:50,051 --> 00:16:51,444
around the winter of eighth grade.

321
00:16:53,297 --> 00:16:55,617
Suzu and I were in the same
class since seventh grade.

322
00:16:57,317 --> 00:16:59,037
She usually came across as really cheerful,

323
00:16:59,257 --> 00:17:02,097
and kind of an assertive girl.

324
00:17:03,277 --> 00:17:05,077
I like you.

325
00:17:07,496 --> 00:17:08,996
So, um...

326
00:17:11,717 --> 00:17:13,836
please go out with me.

327
00:17:15,581 --> 00:17:17,768
[To Watarai-kun]

328
00:17:19,236 --> 00:17:20,236
Back then,

329
00:17:20,817 --> 00:17:22,797
she was more nervous
than I'd ever seen her.

330
00:17:24,337 --> 00:17:25,337
Okay.

331
00:17:28,897 --> 00:17:30,717
Though even if we called it dating,

332
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:32,907
we were still just in middle school.

333
00:17:34,397 --> 00:17:35,997
We'd just walk home from school together

334
00:17:36,737 --> 00:17:38,277
and hang out around the neighborhood.

335
00:17:40,237 --> 00:17:42,877
In middle school, it just felt
like an extension of being friends.

336
00:17:44,237 --> 00:17:45,237
However...

337
00:17:49,986 --> 00:17:52,505
After starting high school,
Suzu got into Instagram.

338
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:56,866
Hey, look.

339
00:17:57,697 --> 00:17:59,657
It's a photo of the earrings
you got me, Tsukasa.

340
00:17:59,704 --> 00:18:01,197
It got so many likes!

341
00:18:02,877 --> 00:18:03,666
I see.

342
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:04,749
Yeah.

343
00:18:05,257 --> 00:18:08,922
Everyone says you're the best
boyfriend, so handsome and sweet.

344
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:10,664
They're all so jealous of me.

345
00:18:11,299 --> 00:18:14,179
After that, she was always glued to
her phone whenever we were together.

346
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:19,307
I realized she probably
didn't actually like me,

347
00:18:19,390 --> 00:18:21,750
she just liked the version of
herself when she was with me.

348
00:18:22,377 --> 00:18:26,455
So, in the summer of freshman
year, I broke up with her.

349
00:18:28,197 --> 00:18:31,457
If you ask me whether
I ever truly loved Suzu,

350
00:18:33,617 --> 00:18:35,197
honestly, I still don't really know.

351
00:18:36,577 --> 00:18:38,297
I did try to love her.

352
00:18:42,737 --> 00:18:44,037
But...

353
00:18:44,677 --> 00:18:46,357
the first person I ever fell for on my own

354
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,644
was you, Hioki.

355
00:18:49,927 --> 00:18:50,927
Huh?

356
00:18:51,957 --> 00:18:53,257
Did I never tell you?

357
00:18:55,637 --> 00:18:57,337
The only person I've ever loved this much

358
00:18:58,457 --> 00:18:59,697
is you.

359
00:19:02,317 --> 00:19:03,617
Only me...

360
00:19:04,397 --> 00:19:05,397
Yeah.

361
00:19:07,057 --> 00:19:08,397
The one who made my heart race,

362
00:19:09,257 --> 00:19:11,597
who made me chase after
them, wanting to know everything,

363
00:19:14,457 --> 00:19:15,957
who made me jealous,

364
00:19:18,323 --> 00:19:19,623
and even lose control...

365
00:19:21,023 --> 00:19:22,323
It's only ever been you, Hioki.

366
00:19:23,736 --> 00:19:25,036
My first love

367
00:19:26,717 --> 00:19:28,017
is you.

368
00:19:42,897 --> 00:19:45,437
I've decided I'm going
to meet Suzu-san after all.

369
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:49,396
Huh?

370
00:19:52,177 --> 00:19:53,234
Are you sure?

371
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:57,229
I don't know if she'll believe us,

372
00:19:58,457 --> 00:20:00,366
but I think it'll be fine.

373
00:20:00,389 --> 00:20:01,932
Even Tsumugi picked up on it.

374
00:20:03,497 --> 00:20:04,497
Tsumugi?

375
00:20:04,829 --> 00:20:05,829
Yeah.

376
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:09,167
Hey,

377
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:10,543
Asahi-kun.

378
00:20:11,502 --> 00:20:15,339
Tsukasa-kun really
likes you, doesn't he?

379
00:20:17,987 --> 00:20:18,987
Yeah.

380
00:20:19,317 --> 00:20:20,617
He does.

381
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:24,213
What about you, Asahi-kun?

382
00:20:25,957 --> 00:20:28,437
You like Tsukasa-kun too, right?

383
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:32,939
Yeah.

384
00:20:36,297 --> 00:20:37,297
I really

385
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:40,281
like him, too.

386
00:20:53,237 --> 00:20:54,914
Besides, even if

387
00:20:54,997 --> 00:20:56,617
we can't prove it,

388
00:20:58,597 --> 00:20:59,967
I really do

389
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:02,027
want to be by your side, Watarai.

390
00:21:02,677 --> 00:21:04,037
That's how I feel.

391
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:07,183
As your boyfriend.

392
00:21:18,997 --> 00:21:19,997
Oh!

393
00:21:20,597 --> 00:21:22,137
I just had a great idea.

394
00:21:23,317 --> 00:21:24,317
Come with me.

395
00:21:33,377 --> 00:21:34,533
We're gonna use this as proof?

396
00:21:34,557 --> 00:21:35,274
Yep.

397
00:21:35,357 --> 00:21:36,394
What do you think?

398
00:21:36,477 --> 00:21:37,854
Hard to say...

399
00:21:37,937 --> 00:21:39,137
Who cares? Let's just take it.

400
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:44,512
Smile, smile!

401
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:45,930
Let's take one more.

402
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:47,013
Okay.

403
00:21:50,617 --> 00:21:51,737
It's pretty cramped in here.

404
00:21:51,769 --> 00:21:52,895
Stop complaining.

405
00:21:53,397 --> 00:21:54,314
Want to take a kissing photo?

406
00:21:54,397 --> 00:21:55,114
No way.

407
00:21:55,197 --> 00:21:55,794
What's the big deal?

408
00:21:55,877 --> 00:21:57,066
No, no, no...

409
00:22:14,257 --> 00:22:15,334
Are you nervous?

410
00:22:16,417 --> 00:22:17,814
Not at all.

411
00:22:17,897 --> 00:22:18,963
It'll be fine.

412
00:22:22,258 --> 00:22:23,258
Okay.

413
00:22:56,437 --> 00:22:57,902
(Next Episode Preview) (Finally
Meeting the Ex-Girlfriend)

414
00:22:57,927 --> 00:23:00,313
At least I know Tsukasa
better than he does.

415
00:23:00,337 --> 00:23:01,414
What about you, Watarai?

416
00:23:01,497 --> 00:23:03,853
(Their Own Futures) Don't you
have any dreams for the future?

417
00:23:03,877 --> 00:23:04,877
To be with Hioki...

418
00:23:05,426 --> 00:23:06,694
for the rest of my life.

419
00:23:06,777 --> 00:23:07,987
Then it's a promise.

420
00:23:08,577 --> 00:23:09,674
Yeah.

421
00:23:09,757 --> 00:23:11,057
It's a promise.

422
00:23:14,317 --> 00:23:15,357
Sorry to keep you waiting.
